V4 (Loam UI Kit / v0-parity design system) complete.

Task: Loam UI Kit token linter (raw colours, >5 colours, >2 fonts, arbitrary px,
emoji icons, missing alt text, gradients) + `design_lint` agent tool.

Commits on khamis1992/v0-v4 (3 ahead of the manus-parity merge base):
  17b288d feat(design): add Loam UI Kit token linter and design_lint tool (V4)
  da9d6c6 fix(design): exempt every declaration on a shared token-definition line (V4)
  353b506 docs(design): record V4 completion (.jdone)

Deliverables:
- src/design/tokenLint.ts: the linter, with two complementary public views.
  * lintDesignSource(source, options) checks one in-memory TSX/HTML/CSS/JS
    string and returns deterministic 1-based line/column violations plus a
    colour/font summary. It never executes the input and never touches disk.
  * minimalDesignLinter() walks a generated site directory and returns a 0-100
    score, a compact issue list and metrics for the design eval harness.
  * Rules: raw-colour, too-many-colours (>5), too-many-fonts (>2),
    arbitrary-px, emoji-icon, missing-alt, gradient, plus two RTL rules
    (rtl-logical-properties, rtl-direction).
  * Token definitions (CSS custom properties) are exempt by default, and one
    shared `tokenRanges` array feeds the raw-colour rule, the palette counter
    and the summary count so the three views cannot drift.
- src/tools/designLint.ts: the `design_lint` agent tool. Accepts either
  `source` + optional `fileName`, or `paths` (files/directories walked
  recursively with an explicit extension allow-list). Read-only, bounded
  (40 files, 200 KB/file, 4 s walk budget), reports skipped paths instead of
  failing silently, and honours maxColours/maxFonts/allowedColours/disabled.
- src/modes/designRules.ts: DESIGN_LINT_PROMPT, injected into the system
  prompt so the model knows the linter exists and which categories it emits.
- src/modes/buildPhases.ts + src/server/runTools.ts: `design_lint` is required
  in the build phases that produce UI and is always-on for the model.
- src/index.ts: registers createDesignLintTools() in the tool registry.

Acceptance test (met):
- src/design/__tests__/tokenLint.test.ts declares exactly 15 fixture cases and
  asserts each one's pass/fail verdict and exact violation categories:
  clean-token-page (pass), raw-tailwind-utility, inline-hex, named-colour,
  rgb-colour, too-many-colours, five-colours-within-limit, too-many-fonts,
  two-fonts-ok (pass), arbitrary-px-text, arbitrary-px-width, emoji-icon,
  img-missing-alt, img-with-alt (pass), gradient.
- src/tools/__tests__/designLint.test.ts covers the tool surface, the
  filesystem walk and the prompt/registration wiring.
- src/design/__tests__/evalDesign.test.ts covers the site-directory linter and
  the eval harness integration.

Tests (all pass from the worktree root):
  npx tsc --noEmit                                   -> exit 0
  npm run build:server                               -> exit 0 (dist/server.cjs)
  (cd packages/web && npx next build)                -> exit 0 (24/24 static pages)
  node --import tsx --test src/design/__tests__/tokenLint.test.ts \
      src/tools/__tests__/designLint.test.ts \
      src/design/__tests__/evalDesign.test.ts         -> 81 pass, 0 fail
  node --import tsx --test src/server/__tests__/runTools.test.ts \
      src/tools/__tests__/designExplore.test.ts \
      src/tools/__tests__/designStudio.test.ts        -> 39 pass, 0 fail

Notes:
- The earlier interrupted session resolved a stale MERGE_HEAD (the merge
  resolution was already committed as 17b288d) and fixed the failing acceptance
  test in da9d6c6; this session re-verified the whole task end to end.
- Arabic/RTL quality is part of the linter: Arabic content without dir="rtl"
  is flagged, physical directional properties (ml-*/mr-*/pl-*/pr-*/text-left,
  margin-left, ...) are flagged under an RTL layout with the logical replacement
  suggested, and the site linter reports rtlReady only when the root declares
  dir="rtl" and the source uses logical properties.
- No existing test was weakened or deleted; only V4's own files are committed.
- The pre-existing staged index pile from other workstreams is left untouched;
  only .jdone is added by this session.
